{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Java vs Java Script", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about Java and JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Explain briefly how different programming languages work.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "programmer ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person in charge of writing codes in order to program computers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A programmer uses Java to change text code into a formatted smaller language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "therefore ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to introduce a consequence or result from a previously described situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Java works on its own while JavaScript has to be located inside an HTML document. Java is, therefore, larger than JavaScript and it uses a more complicated language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "firstly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at the beginning, before anything else, to begin with", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was firstly known as LiveScript and alongside HTML and CSS, it is one of the most important elements of WWW content creation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "while ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that corresponds in a particular manner, at the same time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(conjunction)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Java works on its own while JavaScript has to be located inside an HTML document.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "average ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "typical, normal, regular", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: JavaScript is the easiest programming language for the average software programmer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "on the other hand ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in opposition to, in contrast to", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(connector)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On the other hand, with JavaScript the programmer can alter the program multiple times since it is more independent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for more information comparing Java and JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down similarities and differences between both of them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a mind map or a graphic explaining your findings.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I find more information about programming languages. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read texts about Java and JavaScript.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I organize information graphically.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Use of Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>comparatives</strong> when we want to contrast two nouns. In order to do that, we usually add the suffix <b>-er</b> to the adjective; but we can also use <strong>more</strong> and <strong>both</strong>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We add the suffix <strong><i>-er</i></strong> to most two-syllable adjectives in order to make a comparison between two nouns. However, it is really important to take into account some ortographic considerations:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives with one or two syllables.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tall<strong><i>er</i></strong></br> Small<strong><i>er</i></strong></br> Fast<strong><i>er</i></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives with one or two syllables ending in e.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nice<strong><i>r</i></strong></br> Large<strong><i>r</i></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending with one or two syllables in y.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Prett<strong><i>ier</i></strong><br> Eas<strong><i>ier</i></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We double the last consonant with one or two syllable adjectives ending in a consonant-vowel-consonat combination.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hot<strong><i>ter</i></strong></br> Big<strong><i>ger</i></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"With adjectives that have more than two syllables, we use \u201c<strong><i>more</i></strong>\u201d.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>More</i></strong> beautiful</br> <strong><i>More</i></strong> interesting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular adjectives that are irregular so they change completely.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Good - <strong><i>Better</i></strong></br> Bad - <strong><i>Worse</i></strong></br> Far - <strong><i>Further</i></strong>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<i>Examples:</br> This computer is small<strong>er</strong> than the one I had last year, but it is also fast<strong>er</strong>. </br> This program is <strong>more</strong> interesting and it is also eas<strong>ier</strong> to use.</br></br>  Sometimes we use \u201c<strong>both</strong>\u201d to introduce two nouns in order to compare them:</br></br>  Example: </br> <strong>Both</strong> Java and JavaScript are good, but I guess that Java script is <strong>better</strong>.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Java is older than JavaScript; it was created in 1991 by James Gosling of Sun Microsystems as an object oriented programming. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "JavaScript is composed by a simpler and smaller set of instructions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Both programming languages are also different in the way they show the language to the end user.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Use of Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>superlatives</strong> when we want to compare one noun with two or more nouns of the same kind. We use them to put a noun over the rest or over the general. In order to do that, we usually use <strong>the</strong> and we add the suffix <strong>-est</strong> to the adjective.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We add the suffix -<strong><i>est</i></strong> to most two-syllable adjectives in order to form a superlative structure. However, it is really important to take into account some spelling considerations:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives with one or two syllables.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>The</i></strong> tall<strong><i>est</i></strong></br> <strong><i>The</i></strong> small<strong><i>est</i></strong></br> <strong><i>The</i></strong> fast<strong><i>est</i></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives with one or two syllables ending in e.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>The</i></strong> nic<strong><i>est</i></strong></br> <strong><i>The</i></strong> larg<strong><i>est</i></strong></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives with one or two syllables ending in y.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>The</i></strong> prett<strong><i>iest</i></strong></br> <strong><i>The</i></strong> eas<strong><i>iest</i></strong></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We double the last consonant with adjectives with one or two syllables ending in a consonant-vowel-consonat combination.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>The</i></strong> hot<strong><i>test</i></strong></br> <strong><i>The</i></strong> big<strong><i>gest</i></strong></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"With adjectives formed by more that two syllables we use \u201c<strong>the most</strong>\u201d.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong><i>The most</i></strong> beautiful</br> <strong><i>The most</i></strong> interesting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular adjectives that change completely.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Good - <strong><i>The best</i></strong></br> Bad - <strong><i>The worst</i></strong></br> Far - <strong><i>The furthest</i></strong>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<i> Examples:<br> This computer is <strong>the</strong> small<strong>est</strong> I've ever had, but surprinsigly it is also <strong>the</strong> fast<strong>est</strong> of them all.</br> This program is <strong>the most</strong> interesting of the three an it is also <strong>the</strong> eas<strong>iest</strong> to use.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What is the biggest difference between Java and JavaScript?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We could say that JavaScript is the easiest programming language for the average software programmer.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can compare Java and JavaScript.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can explain why both, java and java script are different.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give examples to show the differences of both programming languages.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you use Java or JavaScript when programming? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you know about the most popular programming languages?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "t