": "Create a poster explaining the differences and similarities between Java and JavaScript.", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n4le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "Good morning everyone! I am Professor George Williams and today's lecture is about Java and JavaScript. We know that they are both similar, but at the same time, they are very different. Some people think that these two programming languages are simply the best; while some other people think that there are better programming languages. </br></br>Java is older than JavaScript; it was created in 1991 by James Gosling of Sun Microsystems as an object-oriented programming language. JavaScript is a more dynamic and interpreted scripting language that was created in 1993 by Netscape. It was firstly known as LiveScript and alongside HTML and CSS; it is one of the most important elements of WWW content creation.", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "59000", "text": "Even though both Java and JavaScript are OOP languages, they are quite distant in terms of their programming structures. For instance, JavaScript is comprised by a simpler and smaller set of instructions. Basically, we could say that JavaScript is the easiest programming language for the average software programmer.</br></br>What is the biggest difference between Java and JavaScript? The most important difference is that Java works on its own while JavaScript has to be located inside an HTML document. Java is, therefore, larger than JavaScript and it uses a more complicated language.", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "104000", "text": "Both programming languages are also different in the way they show the language to the end user; while Java is arranged as \"machine language\", JavaScript is a \u201ctext-based language\u201d. A programmer uses Java to change text code into a formatted smaller language, making impossible to add or subtract anything without destroying the program. On the other hand, with JavaScript the programmer can alter the program multiple times since it is more independent. </br></br>\nThere are many things we didn't say, but I guess this is the best way to start. Any questions so far?", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le03ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}